      {
        "key": "b",
        "label": "(b)",
        "source": {
          "qp": 5
        },
        "stem": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Two inbred varieties of maize, SKV50 and CML153, were crossed. The resulting F1 hybrids were self‑crossed to produce F2 offspring. The F2 plants were grown, and the percentage area of leaf damage caused by <i>E.</i> <i>turcicum</i> was measured.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 5
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Fig. 2.1 shows the results for the F2 generation. The arrows show the mean percentage area of leaf damage for the two parent varieties.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 5
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "figure",
            "id": "fig2.1",
            "caption": "Fig. 2.1",
            "src": "figures/q2_fig2_1.png",
            "alt": "Leaf damage on maize plants",
            "source": {
              "qp": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "parts": [
          {
            "key": "b.i",
            "label": "(i)",
            "source": {
              "qp": 5,
              "ms": 9
            },
            "stem": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Explain how Fig. 2.1 can be used to determine which parent maize variety shows the greatest resistance to infection by <i>E.</i> <i>turcicum</i>.",
                "source": {
                  "qp": 5
                }
              }
            ],
            "marks": 2,
            "topics": [
              {
                "ref": "17.1(1)",
                "role": "primary"
              }
            ],
            "markScheme": {
              "marks": 2,
              "instruction": "<i>any </i><b><i>two</i></b><i> from: </i>",
              "guidance": [],
              "points": [
                {
                  "n": 1,
                  "text": "<b>1 </b> <b> </b> low percentage leaf damage means high resistance (to infection)<b> ; </b>",
                  "numberedInMs": false
                },
                {
                  "n": 2,
                  "text": "<b>2 </b> <b> </b> SKV50 = 22% <u>and</u><b> </b>CML153 = 58%<b> ; </b>",
                  "numberedInMs": false
                },
                {
                  "n": 3,
                  "text": "<b>3 </b> <b> </b> SKV50 shows greater resistance (to infection)<b> ; </b>",
                  "numberedInMs": false
                }
              ]
            },
            "er": [],
            "aiSupplement": {
              "explanation": [
                {
                  "text": "A phenotype may reflect both inherited differences and environmental conditions. Similar genotypes can produce different outcomes in different environments.",
                  "refs": [
                    "syllabus:17.1(1)",
                    "ms:b.i#1"
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "reasoningChain": [
                "Separate genetic and environmental contributions.",
                "Use the stated conditions to explain their combined effect."
              ],
              "inferredMistakes": [
                {
                  "text": "Assuming that all observed variation is inherited",
                  "basis": "inferred",
                  "refs": [
                    "syllabus:17.1(1)"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "type": "short"
          },
          {
            "key": "b.ii",
            "label": "(ii)",
            "source": {
              "qp": 5,
              "ms": 9
            },
            "stem": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "State the name of the type of variation shown by the maize F2 generation in Fig. 2.1.",
                "source": {
                  "qp": 5
                }
              }
            ],
            "marks": 1,
            "topics": [
              {
                "ref": "17.1(2)",
